# A store that nothing reads still keeps its value alive. Nobody can tell that the value was let go unless somebody sees when it, or something that it refers to, is collected:
# the target of a weak reference or of a registry, whatever may be the unknown object, an instance of a built-in class that refers to more than flow sees. Such a field is not published as never read.
# What the value refers to only by way of the one object that has the field does not count: that object keeps it alive without the field
# RUN: flow
# CHECK: field L0.0 "keep" {{*}}initialization=SetAtCreation isUnchangedDuringActivation=true mayKeepObservedObjectAlive=true
# CHECK: field L1.0 "keep" {{*}}initialization=SetAtCreation isUnchangedDuringActivation=true mayKeepObservedObjectAlive=true
# CHECK: field L2.0 "keep" {{*}}initialization=SetAtCreation isUnchangedDuringActivation=true mayKeepObservedObjectAlive=true
